"49b0d6a6-f82d-e841-96d8-5c3e3caa27a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fork is the central claim made concrete: the magnetic field of a moment \
and the field gradient of a charge are the same tensor, contracted with \
different sources. H-bond and dispersion measures ride the seam between the \
two doorways. ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow] grounds: the two branches of the calculator library, \
each a contraction of the one kernel.",
  FontSlant->Italic]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"873a94a8-4dfc-5847-b5b9-8b6249bfc8ca"],

Cell["Rung 6 \[LongDash] Back to shielding: the Ramsey sum", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e378ddc1-a46a-d041-b34b-b19c3b1f1e68"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shielding is the field the electron currents make when the applied field \
stirs them up (Ramsey 1950). The through-space part of the shielding tensor \
at nucleus i is the sum, over nearby sources s, of each source's kernel \
weighted by its intensity. The magnetic mechanisms add a field at the \
nucleus; the electric mechanisms perturb the electronic response. Both enter \
as a contraction of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "D_{ab}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fd6ae4b1-1f4e-234a-82cf-babc109c28a2"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           StyleBox["i", "TI"], ")"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde] ", 
         UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
          StyleBox["s", "TI"], LimitsPositioning -> True], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["s", "TI"]], " ", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["r", FontSlant -> "Bold"], 
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], ")"}], "."}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\sigma_{ab}(i) \\;\\approx\\; \\sum_s I_s\\,D_{ab}(\\mathbf{r}_{is}).",
      "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "079aeed6-e0eb-bc44-85ef-0be2034290b8"],
 "The cell places two sources at different sites, each contributing its own \
kernel about the nucleus, and forms their weighted sum. The sum is still \
symmetric and still traceless, so the rank-2 anisotropic structure survives \
the summation: many sources add up to one tensor of the same shape, never to \
a scalar. The cell then contracts a single axial source onto its own axis and \
recovers the ring-current angular factor, the McConnell law (1 \[Minus] 3cos\
\.b2\[Theta])/\[Rho]\.b3, which is minus the contraction of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "D_{ab}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c9cb8875-e9a7-5743-80ee-c7e95bb3d59b"],
 " (McConnell 1957). "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bac9a69a-7a44-0347-abce-3b1fb01d7a34"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Dsource", "[", "r0_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "=", 
        RowBox[{"coords", "-", "r0"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"n", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"coords", "-", "r0"}], ")"}], " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"coords", "-", "r0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"3", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "a", "]"}], "]"}], "/", "n"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "b", "]"}], "]"}], "/", "n"}], ")"}]}], "-", 
          RowBox[{"KroneckerDelta", "[", 
           RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"n", "^", "3"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"b", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sigma", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Ione", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Dsource", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"a0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"Itwo", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Dsource", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "b0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "   ", 
  
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"sum_s", " ", "I_s", " ", "D_ab", 
    RowBox[{"(", "r_is", ")"}]}], " ", "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sumSymmetric", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{"sigma", "-", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "sigma", "]"}]}], "]"}], "===", 
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sumTraceless", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "sigma", "]"}], "]"}], "===", "0"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"McConnell", " ", "ring"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"current", " ", 
     RowBox[{"factor", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "the", " ", "axial", " ", "diagonal", " ", "of", " ", "D"}]}]}]}], " ", 
   "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mcc", "=", 
    RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Dsource", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ")"}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "      ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "->", 
         RowBox[{"r", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "th", "]"}]}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"y", "->", "0"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"z", "->", 
         RowBox[{"r", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "th", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<sum stays symmetric\>\"", "->", "sumSymmetric"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<sum stays traceless\>\"", "->", "sumTraceless"}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<McConnell factor n.D.n\>\"", "->", "mcc"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",\
ExpressionUUID->"b3eed0ab-56e3-cf4a-a56d-299086db8392"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The loop closes here. Maxwell's source equations became Poisson equations; \
the Poisson operator was inverted by 1/\[Rho]; the second derivative of 1/\
\[Rho] was the kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "D_{ab}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a081b150-2ae0-6343-8dfc-704982686e9d"],
 "; the kernel's geometry gave the magic angle and the (3cos\.b2\[Theta] \
\[Minus] 1)/\[Rho]\.b3 law; the kernel forked into a magnetic and an electric \
doorway; and the doorways sum back into the shielding tensor. Each calculator \
computes one term of the final sum. ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow] grounds: the whole library at once \[LongDash] the \
sum is the calculators added together, each term one source read through the \
one kernel.",
  FontSlant->Italic]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"965edec3-5cdb-7e4b-b2b7-202784078ce7"],

Cell["The chain, closed", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2878aeca-d930-6740-8b6a-9e3f84c4d856"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The tower is now a theorem rather than a slogan. Maxwell \[RightArrow] 1/\
\[Rho] \[RightArrow] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "D_{ab}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "944e86e3-3c9a-c14d-b3e9-bc88e5a43a9f"],
 " \[RightArrow] the fork \[RightArrow] the calculators \[RightArrow] \
shielding holds at every rung, and each rung is checked above in the kernel. \
The classical calculators are not formulas the thesis trusts; they are the \
only thing they could have been, named projections of one geometry that is \
the near-field shadow of Maxwell. "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46f515a2-b219-8446-8e62-dcb3c93ffe10"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"20a65771-2f7f-e048-a29e-cedec24aa465"],

